## Why This Is Asked

Tests basic streaming ingestion, Pub/Sub, Cloud Functions, and BigQuery interaction; checks ability to implement idempotent writes with insertId; ensures knowledge of minimal IAM and basic test planning.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub ingestion and ordering
- Cloud Functions for schema validation
- BigQuery insertId for deduplication
- IAM minimally scoped
- Test plan including duplicates and invalid messages

## Code Example

```javascript
const {BigQuery} = require('@google-cloud/bigquery');
const bigquery = new BigQuery();

exports.ingestSensor = async (message, context) => {
  const data = Buffer.from(message.data, 'base64').toString();
  let parsed;
  try { parsed = JSON.parse(data); } catch (e) { return; }
  if (!parsed.device || typeof parsed.ts === 'undefined' || typeof parsed.value !== 'number') {
    return;
  }
  const insertId = `${message.id}_${parsed.device}_${parsed.ts}`;
  await bigquery.dataset('iot').table('readings').insert([Object.assign({}, parsed, {insertId})]);
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency and ensure dedup when messages are out of order?
- How would you adapt this to handle schema evolution changes or late-arriving data?

